# Design-First UI Gate

For every app UI task, treat `设计稿/` as the visual source of truth and `设计稿/README.md` as the required workflow. Existing code and product docs remain authoritative for behavior, data, security, and platform constraints.

Before editing UI source:

1. Open and visually inspect every relevant reference image; filenames alone are insufficient.
2. Publish a style lock naming scope, theme, exact files, visual invariants, retained behavior, unknowns, and planned acceptance screenshots.
3. Begin implementation only after the lock is recorded.

Use detail image > same-theme full-page image > `主设计稿.png`. Never combine glass and healing visuals into a third style. `design-demos/` and the current UI may fill unspecified gaps but cannot override `设计稿/`.

If theme, scope, conflicting references, or a material state is ambiguous, ask the user before coding. Re-lock when the user changes the target or references.

Preserve behavior and real product copy unless explicitly changed. Verify the result with same-theme, same-state screenshots at the target window size, relevant checks, and documented intentional deviations.
